12:    - The marker color appears exactly as a solid 2x2 square.
13:    - Source pixels lie in one or more quadrants around that marker square.
14:
15:    Rule
16:    - Use the center of the 2x2 marker square as both a horizontal and vertical
17:      mirror axis.
18:    - For every source pixel, paint its vertical reflection, horizontal
19:      reflection, and 180-degree reflection in the same source color.
20:
21:    Key insight
22:    - The green 2x2 square is not copied; it defines the mirror center for a
23:      four-way reflection closure of the red mask.
24:    """
